1	/**
2	 * fleet/operator-spawn — the operator→agent spawn engine over the durable nursery
3	 * (Brief 4, agent-briefs-2026-06-05; findings folded into
4	 * autoloop-pot-operator-rebuild-2026-06-05).
5	 *
6	 * The one spawn path the operator (chat `<spawn>` tag, the `fleet:spawn` tool, and
7	 * any future admin trigger) goes through:
8	 *
9	 *   resolveProject(harness) → recordSpawn (harness_shared.spawned_agents)
10	 *     → spawnInvokeOnce in the background → finishSpawn on exit.
11	 *
12	 * Replaces the dead POST /api/plugins/orchestrator/spawn dispatch (the
13	 * @papercupai/orchestrator-spawn plugin is not installed, so its projected HTTP
14	 * path 404s and its tracking lived in a plugin-local in-memory Map that
15	 * fleet:tree could not see). Tracking here is the SAME durable nursery the
16	 * fleet:* tools read — what's spawned appears in fleet:tree immediately and the
17	 * row transitions running→done/failed when the child exits.
18	 *
19	 * Resolution failures are recorded as status='failed' nursery rows (with the
20	 * error in error_message) rather than dropped — the old path's silent
